  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> are two fixed vertices of <math><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the vertex <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> moves in the first quadrant in such a way that <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2,</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> then the locus of the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
